From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] target/i386: decode outside the function that calls
 sigsetjmp

Under Emscripten without WebAssembly exceptions, a function that calls
setjmp makes every call it contains through a JavaScript invoke_* wrapper
that catches longjmp, and checks the function's setjmp table after each
one.  disas_insn() calls sigsetjmp() for its two longjmps (an instruction
too long, a page crossed in the middle of one), and the compiler inlined
the whole decoder into it and it into i386_tr_translate_insn(): the dozens
of calls to tcg_gen_*() and the gen_* helpers that translating one guest
instruction makes all went through JavaScript, and the function grew to
196772 bytes of WebAssembly.  JavaScriptCore never compiles a function
body over Options::maximumOMGCandidateCost bytes (40000 in WebKit 2.48,
100000 since) with its optimizing tier, so in Safari the translator ran as
baseline code for good.

The decoder is now disas_insn_body(), noinline, called from disas_insn()
after the sigsetjmp(): one call per guest instruction goes through
JavaScript, and a longjmp from the decoder still lands in disas_insn().
setjmp_gen_code() is noinline for the same reason, so that only its own
calls, not all of tb_gen_code()'s, are made through JavaScript.
---
diff --git a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
index 87324bc..310e7e3 100644
--- a/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
+++ b/accel/tcg/translate-all.c
@@ -264,8 +264,12 @@ void page_init(void)
 /*
  * Isolate the portion of code gen which can setjmp/longjmp.
  * Return the size of the generated code, or negative on error.
+ *
+ * Porty: noinline, or under Emscripten every call of tb_gen_code() would
+ * go through a JavaScript invoke_* wrapper (see disas_insn_body() in
+ * target/i386/tcg/translate.c).
  */
-static int setjmp_gen_code(CPUArchState *env, TranslationBlock *tb,
+static int __attribute__((noinline)) setjmp_gen_code(CPUArchState *env, TranslationBlock *tb,
                            vaddr pc, void *host_pc,
                            int *max_insns, int64_t *ti)
 {
diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
index 037bc47..9020c97 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/translate.c
@@ -3059,15 +3059,25 @@ static void gen_cmpxchg16b(DisasContext *s, CPUX86State *env, int modrm)
 }
 #endif
 
+/*
+ * Porty: the decoder proper, out of disas_insn(), which calls sigsetjmp().
+ * Under Emscripten (without WebAssembly exceptions) a function that calls
+ * setjmp makes every call it contains through a JavaScript invoke_*
+ * wrapper that catches longjmp, followed by a check of the setjmp table.
+ * With the decoder inlined into disas_insn() (and that into
+ * i386_tr_translate_insn()), each of the dozens of calls to tcg_gen_*()
+ * and the gen_* helpers per guest instruction went through JavaScript, and
+ * the function had grown to 197 KB, which JavaScriptCore never compiles
+ * with its optimizing tier (Options::maximumOMGCandidateCost, 40000 or
+ * 100000 bytes).  Now one call per instruction goes through JavaScript;
+ * a longjmp from the decoder (advance_pc()) still lands in disas_insn().
+ */
+static bool disas_insn_body(DisasContext *s, CPUState *cpu);
+
 /* convert one instruction. s->base.is_jmp is set if the translation must
    be stopped. Return the next pc value */
 static bool disas_insn(DisasContext *s, CPUState *cpu)
 {
-    CPUX86State *env = cpu_env(cpu);
-    int b, prefixes;
-    int shift;
-    MemOp ot, aflag, dflag;
-    int modrm, reg, rm, mod, op, opreg, val;
     bool orig_cc_op_dirty = s->cc_op_dirty;
     CCOp orig_cc_op = s->cc_op;
     target_ulong orig_pc_save = s->pc_save;
@@ -3108,6 +3118,16 @@ static bool disas_insn(DisasContext *s, CPUState *cpu)
     default:
         g_assert_not_reached();
     }
+    return disas_insn_body(s, cpu);
+}
+
+static bool __attribute__((noinline)) disas_insn_body(DisasContext *s, CPUState *cpu)
+{
+    CPUX86State *env = cpu_env(cpu);
+    int b, prefixes;
+    int shift;
+    MemOp ot, aflag, dflag;
+    int modrm, reg, rm, mod, op, opreg, val;
 
     prefixes = 0;
 
